# What gets uploaded to Vercel.
#
# Two problems this solves, both found by running a real build:
#
# 1. Without it the static layer serves the whole repository — data/, uploads/, tests/,
#    logs, the removed scaffold — at the deployment's URL.
# 2. `.env.local` was being pulled into the function bundle. It holds the project's OIDC
#    token, so that is a credential in a build artifact.

tests/
scripts/
docs/
data/
uploads/
.vercel_python_packages/
.vercel/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
run.bat
run_studio.py
requirements-dev.txt
BUGS.md.old
PLAN.md.old
QUICKSTART.md
TESTING.md
DESIGN_REVIEW.md
ENGINEERING_REPORT.md
.opencode/
.claude/
